1
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:14,280
The End

2
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:17,420
North latitude 28 degrees 24 minutes.

3
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:20,880
West longitude 80 degrees 36 minutes.

4
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:25,180
Go there, and wait patiently
for the next new moon.

5
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:28,200
That, my friend, is when heaven will come.

6
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:31,597
I have no further use for this prison.

7
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:35,320
The child that was born is
already in my possession.

8
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:38,078
Here's the story of Jailhouse Locke.

9
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:41,817
Try as you might, you can only
remember three things at a time.

10
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:43,900
I know I need something, but what?

11
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:45,040
What's important?

12
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:47,037
What's something I cannot forget?

13
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:51,260
I have something important to tell
Jolene. I gotta go. She needs me.

14
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:56,140
Wait a minute.

15
00:00:56,420 --> 00:00:57,949
What the hell was I doing?

16
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:00,770
Hmm...

17
00:01:00,853 --> 00:01:01,683
something...

18
00:01:01,766 --> 00:01:02,596
isn't right.

19
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:08,590
Wait, what?

20
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:10,447
That doesn't make any sense.

21
00:01:10,540 --> 00:01:12,599
Why would he go into that building?

22
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:14,646
I don't understand this show!

23
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:16,060
Just let it play!

24
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:18,637
Why do you always have to keep
on doing what you're doing?

25
00:01:18,720 --> 00:01:19,737
Take the remote from her!

26
00:01:19,820 --> 00:01:21,397
I don't know what the
fuck is happening anymore!

27
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:23,237
And drag her dumb ass out of here!

28
00:01:23,320 --> 00:01:24,150
Huh?

29
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:26,077
Fine, I won't watch it then.

30
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:26,990
You happy now?

31
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:30,640
All right, newbie.

32
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:33,311
That there spider's the boss of this cell.

33
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:36,240
Oh, hey, good to meet you, man.

34
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:37,677
Hope we can get along.

35
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:39,580
They call me Ron the Viper.

36
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:43,440
Oh, uh, yeah, of course. Appreciate it.

37
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:46,737
And that spider over there
is on the brink of death.

38
00:01:46,820 --> 00:01:48,320
Yo, sup, bro?

39
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:51,100
What is this?

40
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:53,897
How the hell is any of
this supposed to be funny?

41
00:01:53,980 --> 00:01:55,717
Man, this comic book is a mess.

42
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:57,094
I don't get it at all.

43
00:01:57,660 --> 00:01:59,180
Where am I? The rec room?

44
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:02,086
I must have had a good
reason to come in here.

45
00:02:05,460 --> 00:02:08,140
Oh yeah, I have to go see Emporio.

46
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:12,284
I'm here to find another way to
break out of this place, somehow.

47
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:17,791
There's the medical wing.

48
00:02:18,620 --> 00:02:20,796
Emporio's room is off that staircase.

49
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,737
It's usually a walk in the park,
but they beefed up security today.

50
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:27,340
So how do I get to Emporio in one piece?

51
00:02:49,260 --> 00:02:50,760
Shit! It's a stand!

52
00:02:51,160 --> 00:02:53,717
And I know I've seen it before! The enemy!

53
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:55,380
I've got to go after it!

54
00:02:55,620 --> 00:02:57,149
And that woman's the user!

55
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:28,037
I'm going to move on and
move on The way I'm going

56
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:32,100
to turn around The trap
and hate will be broken

57
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:34,060
Okay? Alright?

58
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:41,940
No survival day Get away from
Go, go, go I don't wanna fade

59
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:48,500
Let's go, go 1, 2, 3 Come
and find a way Rise for me

60
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:56,330
Break out!

61
00:03:56,413 --> 00:03:57,380
We're coming out!

62
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:08,910
Wait a second.

63
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:10,080
Where am I?

64
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:12,357
And who was I chasing after just now?

65
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:14,217
What is happening? I got her!

66
00:05:14,300 --> 00:05:16,359
We're at the corner of hallway D12.

67
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:17,600
You, hands up!

68
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:21,580
Oh no, the one being
chased right now is me!

69
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:25,597
Look, here she comes!

70
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:26,720
Hey, don't move!

71
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:37,817
I could have sworn there were
two guards there a second ago.

72
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:38,780
Who cares?

73
00:05:39,060 --> 00:05:40,337
Doesn't matter right now.

74
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:41,780
What is this place?

75
00:05:42,540 --> 00:05:44,600
Seriously, how did I even get here?

76
00:05:44,860 --> 00:05:46,389
Why are they all after me?

77
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:06,790
Where is she?

78
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:08,517
I knew I saw her head that way.

79
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:09,430
Find her.

80
00:06:09,513 --> 00:06:10,343
Go move your ass.

81
00:06:10,426 --> 00:06:11,697
There's no way she just disappeared.

82
00:06:11,780 --> 00:06:13,617
She's gotta be hiding somewhere close by!

83
00:06:13,700 --> 00:06:15,577
Maybe she ran toward the stairwell!

84
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:16,490
Not a chance.

85
00:06:16,660 --> 00:06:19,357
She would've had to pass right
by us, we'd have seen her.

86
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:20,400
The stairwell?

87
00:06:21,060 --> 00:06:22,460
Go see Emporio.

88
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:24,586
Okay, it's coming back to me.

89
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:27,802
Those are the stairs that
lead to Emporio's room.

90
00:06:43,980 --> 00:06:45,620
What was I doing just now?

91
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:49,380
Oh yeah, I spilled the water
and it went everywhere.

92
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:54,377
There's something I need to tell, Jolene.

93
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:56,931
I have to get to her before it's too late.

94
00:06:57,560 --> 00:07:01,325
But I have to write somewhere
else before I forget it all again.

95
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:03,912
I need to make sure she sees the mugshot.

96
00:07:04,860 --> 00:07:06,937
Or else I won't be able to tell her...

97
00:07:07,020 --> 00:07:08,460
tell her that...

98
00:07:12,280 --> 00:07:16,840
Jolene Kujo, since you can only
retain up to three memories at a time,

99
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:19,517
even if there are four
guards chasing after you,

100
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:22,306
you'll only be able to
remember three of them.

101
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:26,517
Of course, your eyes will be able to see
all of them, totaling more than four,

102
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:29,718
but your brain will outright
reject them as a memory.

103
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:33,157
Go see Emporio.

104
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:35,300
I made you guide me here.

105
00:07:35,900 --> 00:07:36,730
Interesting.

106
00:07:36,813 --> 00:07:39,231
Who'd have thought I'd find a secret room?

107
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:52,590
Emporio?

108
00:07:58,400 --> 00:08:00,340
Jolene, when did you get here?

109
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:01,480
I just showed up.

110
00:08:01,860 --> 00:08:03,117
Oh, look at your hand.

111
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:04,277
Poor you, what happened?

112
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:05,360
This looks awful.

113
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:09,407
Wait, is this because you can
only remember three things, too?

114
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:14,037
My arms have the exact same writing
on them, ever since being in solitary.

115
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:15,900
Oh yeah, I remember now.

116
00:08:16,020 --> 00:08:17,357
I wanted to talk to you, Jolene.

117
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:19,697
There's something really
important I need to tell you.

118
00:08:19,780 --> 00:08:21,880
Are you listening to me? Uh, what?

119
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:23,492
Sorry, what was I doing?

120
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:27,290
Hey, wait.

121
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:28,837
When did you get here, Jolene?

122
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:30,620
And why? Very funny.

123
00:08:30,900 --> 00:08:32,371
Seriously, why am I here?

124
00:08:32,740 --> 00:08:34,120
Why, why, why, why?

125
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:35,640
Oh, that's right.

126
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:37,517
I came to see you, and it's urgent.

127
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:39,080
But I have no idea why.

128
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:42,969
I just knew that if I didn't
come, I'd be up Schitt's Creek.

129
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:44,190
Print it out.

130
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:45,777
Yes, I've got to print it out!

131
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:48,457
And fast, or else I'm
going to forget it forever!

132
00:08:48,540 --> 00:08:50,540
That's the only way I can save it!

133
00:08:50,820 --> 00:08:52,232
Print what out, Emporio?

134
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:54,969
What do you mean when
you say print it out?

135
00:08:56,380 --> 00:08:58,437
How do I, um, what was...

136
00:08:58,520 --> 00:08:59,857
was it again?

137
00:08:59,940 --> 00:09:00,900
Um, let's see.

138
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:03,760
Name, Miu Miu.

139
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,400
Rank, Chief Guard.

140
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:08,380
Oh, I get it.

141
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:12,489
So last time we met, that little
rat was there with you too.

142
00:09:12,780 --> 00:09:16,180
He saw my face and my
stand, and he heard my name.

143
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:19,900
That Emporio was inside the
wall in the solitary cell.

144
00:09:20,740 --> 00:09:22,446
Usually, I'd leave him alone.

145
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:26,097
My jailhouse lock's duty is to
spot who the stand users are,

146
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:28,437
track them down, and make
sure they're locked up.

147
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:30,637
But if there's any
evidence of me out there...

148
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:32,040
That's another story.

149
00:09:32,300 --> 00:09:34,360
So stand down, you jailbreaker!

150
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:43,080
Her stand, Stone Ocean, is too strong.

151
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:45,517
So these bullets will
be useless against her.

152
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:47,659
But I know you won't remember this.

153
00:09:47,780 --> 00:09:49,557
That if I had shot four bullets at you,

154
00:09:49,640 --> 00:09:51,677
you would have no clue
where the last bullet went.

155
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:54,897
You'd piss your pants not knowing
whether it hit you or missed you.

156
00:09:54,980 --> 00:09:59,627
You wouldn't even be able to see or smell
one wisp of smoke from the gunpowder.

157
00:10:01,940 --> 00:10:02,980
J-Jolene...

158
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:04,550
What?!

159
00:10:05,640 --> 00:10:08,477
I don't know why there's a room
nor why there's a kid here.

160
00:10:08,560 --> 00:10:11,117
The whole thing sure
smells suspicious as fuck.

161
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:15,177
Although Palesnake mentions somebody
in here, is in cahoots with Jolene,

162
00:10:15,260 --> 00:10:17,437
scheming and coordinating elaborate escape

163
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:20,285
plans with walkie-talkies
and other technology.

164
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:22,718
He must have been talking about you.

165
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:25,360
And now all the data he collected is gone!

166
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:26,875
What a waste of time!

167
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:27,997
You rotten bitch!

168
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:29,217
I'm gonna make you pay!

169
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:31,480
Huh, such passion.

170
00:10:31,940 --> 00:10:34,217
Too bad, after these next three things,

171
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:37,977
even those fervent emotions will be
as lost as your chance at freedom.

172
00:10:38,060 --> 00:10:40,766
That's the beauty of
what Jailhouse Lock does.

173
00:10:41,080 --> 00:10:42,760
Eat shit, Jolene Cujo!

174
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:44,040
This is the end!

175
00:10:48,220 --> 00:10:51,297
Out of this hail of bullets, you're
only gonna be aware of three.

176
00:10:51,380 --> 00:10:54,615
The rest will pierce your
body like knives into butter!

177
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:10,657
You can try to fuck with my head all
you want, but the reflection won't lie.

178
00:11:10,740 --> 00:11:13,211
No matter how many shots you fire at once,

179
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:16,077
I'm gonna see every single
one of them in the blood.

180
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:19,336
And I'm sure you haven't
forgotten anything, have you?

181
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:30,497
It's too late, I've already
destroyed the computer.

182
00:11:30,580 --> 00:11:32,345
My only choice is to bail out.

183
00:11:32,620 --> 00:11:33,777
What's the difference?

184
00:11:33,860 --> 00:11:36,217
Jolene's gonna forget me in
about two seconds anyway.

185
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:38,947
I'll be forgotten forever,
not even a memory.

186
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:44,797
Emporio, try to hang on a little longer.

187
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:46,468
I'm going after that bitch.

188
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:47,910
I...

189
00:11:47,993 --> 00:11:49,501
I don't think you should, Jolene.

190
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:51,917
We both know you're...

191
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:55,337
you're gonna forget again the
minute you leave this room.

192
00:11:55,420 --> 00:11:58,237
You're even gonna forget that
you'll have to defeat her.

193
00:11:58,320 --> 00:11:59,577
So please...

194
00:11:59,660 --> 00:12:00,640
Emporio, look.

195
00:12:00,780 --> 00:12:02,737
I understand you wanting to be careful.

196
00:12:02,820 --> 00:12:04,120
I like that about you.

197
00:12:04,340 --> 00:12:07,017
How else were you gonna survive
this shit-bucket prison?

198
00:12:07,100 --> 00:12:08,629
You needed to be that way.

199
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:10,140
But still,

200
00:12:10,580 --> 00:12:12,877
eventually it's going to
get to the point where

201
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:15,489
you have to make a move
even if it's risky.

202
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:17,420
So you've got to understand.

203
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:20,400
For me, that time is now!

204
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:23,960
Is this Jolene's thread?

205
00:12:42,060 --> 00:12:43,000
I'm hurt.

206
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:44,632
How'd this happen to me?

207
00:12:46,040 --> 00:12:46,880
But still,

208
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:49,837
eventually it's going to
get to the point where

209
00:12:49,920 --> 00:12:52,449
you have to make a move
even if it's risky.

210
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:55,877
I still don't know what it is.

211
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:58,537
But I know I'm supposed to do
something really important.

212
00:12:58,620 --> 00:12:59,900
Something like…

213
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:01,750
That's right.

214
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:03,473
I have to print it out.

215
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:05,820
That's what I need to tell Jolene.

216
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:08,557
So I'll print it out and…

217
00:13:08,640 --> 00:13:10,140
But what was it again?

218
00:13:10,440 --> 00:13:12,852
What was the thing I'm supposed to print?

219
00:13:13,220 --> 00:13:14,050
What?

220
00:13:14,133 --> 00:13:16,495
I don't even have a printer
in my room, so how can I...

221
00:13:25,860 --> 00:13:27,100
It's so strong!

222
00:13:30,140 --> 00:13:31,380
Yep, she's the enemy.

223
00:13:32,380 --> 00:13:34,909
She's not gonna get
away from me this time!

224
00:13:38,660 --> 00:13:40,117
Come back, I need you!

225
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:42,200
I'm at the stairs at D-10!

226
00:13:46,560 --> 00:13:47,420
I see them!

227
00:13:47,580 --> 00:13:48,517
They're right over there!

228
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:50,482
Chief Beauty was being attacked!

229
00:13:50,900 --> 00:13:52,760
The gate, open it! Hurry up!

230
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:07,760
Wait, where am I? What happened?

231
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:09,115
What am I doing here?

232
00:14:11,220 --> 00:14:12,050
Move it!

233
00:14:12,260 --> 00:14:13,907
Grab her before she escapes!

234
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:15,972
They're chasing someone.

235
00:14:16,540 --> 00:14:17,370
It's me!

236
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:22,517
That's right, I called
the three guards back.

237
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:26,337
Now any and all memories you had of me
are lost forever, just like your freedom.

238
00:14:26,420 --> 00:14:27,250
Oops.

239
00:14:35,220 --> 00:14:36,867
Get up and run a bit, honey.

240
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:40,157
That'll give them more of a reason
to put a bullet in your head.

241
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:42,320
Oh, right, those big, strong arms.

242
00:14:42,500 --> 00:14:45,441
I nearly forgot they can
deflect any shots at you.

243
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:57,751
My official sworn duty is really only
to make sure stand users get put away.

244
00:14:58,220 --> 00:15:01,338
But I'm rather excited you're
getting more than that.

245
00:15:03,980 --> 00:15:06,509
Knowing you're about
to die makes me giddy.

246
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:08,737
If anyone deserves it, it's you.

247
00:15:08,820 --> 00:15:12,820
This is all because you refuse to
behave and be a good little doggy.

248
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:14,320
I got her!

249
00:15:14,480 --> 00:15:18,377
Oh, also, the fact that you can only
see three guards in front of you

250
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:20,280
is driving me wild with joy.

251
00:15:23,660 --> 00:15:28,542
You're never getting past my jailhouse
lock, so you might as well stop fighting it!

252
00:15:31,900 --> 00:15:32,820
Hey, Jolene.

253
00:15:33,300 --> 00:15:34,594
When did you get here?

254
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:36,997
I know you. You're Emporio.

255
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:39,760
Wait, Jolene, you gotta know,

256
00:15:40,160 --> 00:15:44,278
this needs to be printed out or else
I was gonna forget it in no time.

257
00:15:45,060 --> 00:15:46,140
Print what out?

258
00:15:46,500 --> 00:15:47,840
It's in binary code.

259
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:50,257
